knext bundled fix for vinext 1.0.1 (dist output)
Upstream: https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/pull/3687
What it fixes: A next.config.js/.ts exported as a function is invoked with
`(phase, { defaultConfig })` per the Next.js config API. vinext always passed
an empty object for `defaultConfig`, so a config that reads a field off it
(e.g. Next's own custom-page-extension e2e fixture, which does
`pageExtensions: [...defaultConfig.pageExtensions, 'page.js']`) throws
`TypeError: defaultConfig.pageExtensions is not iterable` at build time.
Passes `defaultConfig.pageExtensions` (vinext's own default list, which
matches Next's config-shared.js `defaultConfig.pageExtensions`) at both call
sites: the direct function-config path, and the generated virtual-module
loader used for .ts configs.
Retire: delete this file (and its manifest entry) when the pinned vinext is >= the first
release that includes cloudflare/vinext#3687.
Ported by hand from the upstream src change to the published 1.0.1 dist files.
Applied by `knext vinext-patches` (runs from the app's postinstall and before `knext build`).

